The fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989

Timeline {1980: The wall is first erected. 1984: Protocol on the opening of the wall is signed. 1989: People climb and hammer away at the wall, symbolizing its fall. Nov 9, 1989: Berlin Wall officially comes down. 1990: Partition of German is officially ended.}

Write a function to find the highest number in the given list of integers.

[8, 3, 5, 9, 1]

def findMax(myList):
    maxNum = myList[0]
    for num in myList:
        if num > maxNum:
            maxNum = num
    return maxNum

print(findMax([8, 3, 5, 9, 1])) # Output: 9

Create an algorithm that calculates the factorial of a given number.

N/A

def factorial(n): 
    # Base Case 
    if n == 0: 
        return 1

    # Recursive case 
    return n * factorial(n-1)

Write a c program that takes a string from the user and reverses it

#include<stdio.h> 
#include<string.h> 

// Function to reverse any sequence starting with pointer 
// begin and ending with pointer end 
void Reverse(char* begin, char* end) 
{ 
    char temp; 
    while (begin < end) { 
        temp = *begin; 
        *begin++ = *end; 
        *end-- = temp; 
    } 
} 

// Function to reverse words*/ 
void ReverseWords(char* s) 
{ 
    char* word_begin = s; 

    // Word boundary 
    char* temp = s; 

    // Revert string 
    Reverse(s, temp); 

    // Revert each word 
    while (*temp) { 
        temp++; 
        if (*temp == '\0') { 
            Reverse(word_begin, temp - 1); 
        } else if (*temp == ' ') { 
            Reverse(word_begin, temp - 1); 
            word_begin = temp + 1; 
        } 
    } 
} 

// Driver code 
int main() 
{ 
    char s[] = "Welcome to Geeksforgeeks"; 
    char* temp = s; 
    ReverseWords(s); 
    printf("%s", s); 

    return 0; 
}

